  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Sea Turtle Conservation, Adapting to Climate Change and Assisting CONAP in meeting Guatemalas IAC Commitments</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to implement a sea turtle conservation program in Guatemala. The intent is to protect sea turtles and their nests from poaching and depredation and to assist Government of Guatemala in complying with its obligations under the Inter-American Sea Turtle Convention (IAC) regarding exceptions for sustainable harvest of eggs. Activities include: 1) conducting nest monitoring surveys at eight index beaches to assess long-term population trends; 2) strengthening hatchery management through capacity building workshops to improve hatching success; and 3) working with National Council of Protected Areas (CONANP) and IAC to develop a management plan for sustainable olive ridley egg harvest.</narrative>
  </description>
